    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n67856" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μί̄μ-ησις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>imitation</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				156
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.95
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Grg.</u>
				511a
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ σὴν μ.</span> to
			imitate you, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				109
			</span></i>; <i>reproduction</i> of a model, <i><span class="en">
				Dionys.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Syrian.
				<u>in Hermog.</u>
				1.3
			</span></i> R. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>representation by means of art</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Sph.</u>
				265b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>R.</u>
				598b
			</span></i>, al.; esp. of dramatic poetry, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Po.</u>
				1447a22
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>representation, portrait</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυγμαίου ἀνδρὸς μ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					3.37
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Vict.</u>
				1.21
			</span></i>.</div>
